1
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,880
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,280
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,920
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:22,280
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

5
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:25,520
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

6
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:29,920
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

7
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:34,040
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

8
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:38,840
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

9
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:42,520
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

10
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:48,560
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

11
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,960
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

12
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:55,960
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

13
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:58,720
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

14
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,160
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

15
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:02,720
♪ You cracked my code ♪

16
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,960
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

17
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:09,040
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

18
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:13,840
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

19
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:16,480
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

20
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,280
♪ That says I love you? ♪

21
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,960
♪ Love you ♪

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,960
Every kind of relationship...

23
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,960
has its own set of rules.

24
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:07,200
Rules that were never written down,

25
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:11,520
but we learn them ourselves
through that relationship.

26
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,480
My rule is...

27
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:26,000
never think beyond the status I've been given.

28
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,360
I've always tried to follow that rule.

29
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,800
Because to him,

30
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,360
I can only be his little brother.

31
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,520
(1 month earlier)

32
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,400
Yes.

33
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,600
Yes, Aunt Wan.

34
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,960
Aunt Wan, are you sure you want me
to surprise Kit for his birthday?

35
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,640
Please do it for me, son.

36
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:04,520
Kit doesn't want me getting involved
with his new company these days.

37
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,400
Okay.

38
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:08,440
I'll let him know you sent your regards.

39
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,800
Has my ex really changed?

40
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,840
I didn't do anything to you back then

41
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,040
out of respect.

42
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,880
Not because I didn't know how.

43
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,400
Then prove it.

44
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:41,480
If you'd been like this from the start,

45
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,040
we wouldn't have broken up.

46
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,160
Pat.

47
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,560
Pat, stop. Please, I'm begging you.

48
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,480
Shut up!

49
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,040
Look at yourself.

50
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,040
Go wait in the car.

51
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,280
Pat...

52
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:15,760
Go!

53
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,320
You went after my woman.

54
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:52,680
Kit!

55
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:00,760
Kit!

56
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,200
Kit.

57
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,400
Kit.

58
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,160
Kit.

59
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,920
Kit, wake up. Kit.

60
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,360
Kit, stay with me. Kit.

61
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,320
Kit. Kit.

62
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,640
Aunt Wan.

63
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,440
I can stay with him.

64
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,600
You should go home and get some rest.

65
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:01,840
I won't be able to sleep anyway.

66
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,240
Hello, ma'am.

67
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,720
What do you want?

68
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,680
Commissioner Wit, my uncle,

69
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,200
said there might've been
a little misunderstanding.

70
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,720
So I'm here to clear things up.

71
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,080
He called me directly.

72
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:39,160
But using the word "misunderstanding"
to erase what happened,

73
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,720
isn't that a little too convenient?

74
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,960
My uncle knows me well.

75
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,480
He knows I don't like trouble.

76
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,240
I'm just possessive of my fiancée.

77
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,680
Anyone would feel the same.

78
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,520
If your son hadn't gone after my fiancée,

79
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,280
none of this would've happened.

80
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,400
Mr. Punnapat,

81
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,720
I think you've got it all wrong.

82
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:06,640
Kit isn't like that.

83
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:10,520
But what I saw says otherwise.

84
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,280
You don't even know him.

85
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:16,400
And as for everything that happened,

86
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,280
we have solid evidence.

87
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:21,480
I'm the victim here,

88
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,840
yet I went out of my way to
bring flowers and apologize.

89
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,360
At least give me some credit.

90
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,920
Mr. Punnapat,

91
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,640
listen to me carefully.

92
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,560
Kit would never go back to Cha

93
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,600
because he's my boyfriend.

94
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,520
Are you saying that my future wife

95
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,840
went after your boyfriend?

96
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:52,880
He's not just my boyfriend.

97
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,640
He's my future husband.

98
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,200
I'm Kit's fiancé.

99
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:05,800
Are you so afraid I'll kill him that
you made up this whole same-sex relationship?

100
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,720
We've been in love for a long time.

101
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,800
And we've been planning to get married

102
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:15,920
once marriage equality becomes law.

103
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,040
Whether you believe it or not is up to you.

104
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:28,680
But once my son has recovered,

105
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,800
I will hold the wedding immediately.

106
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,880
Then that's great.

107
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:36,880
In that case, let me congratulate you both.

108
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,480
Whenever you have the wedding,

109
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,600
please send me an invitation.

110
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:46,600
That way, I'll know for sure your son

111
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,560
won't bother my fiancée again.

112
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,360
You were unconscious for a week.
Aunt Wan cried herself to sleep every night.

113
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:10,280
No one knew when you were gonna wake up.

114
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,280
And Punnapat came and threatened to kill you.

115
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:16,080
Do you know how scared I was?!

116
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,560
Huh?!

117
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,680
I won't lose you again.

118
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,400
But it's none of your business.

119
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,120
I can handle my problems by myself!

120
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,200
You can't handle your problems!

121
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,440
That's why I decided to marry you!

122
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,720
I'm an adult now, Kit.

123
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,360
How long are you gonna see me
as your little brother?

124
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,440
Nont, no one forced you

125
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,040
to make this decision, right?

126
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:00,240
No, Auntie. I made the decision myself.

127
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:05,200
Mom, I don't want Nont to get involved in this.

128
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:08,400
Kit, I haven't given you permission to speak.

129
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:15,760
And you didn't use the fact that I took you in

130
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,960
after your family passed away

131
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,920
to make this decision, did you, Nont?

132
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:26,160
Well, about 20%, Auntie.

133
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:30,360
But the other 80% is because
I genuinely want to help Kit.

134
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,160
Kit.

135
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,640
You do know that this wedding we're having

136
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,320
is meant to keep you safe from harm

137
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,080
caused by the mistake you made, right?

138
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,840
Yes, I know.

139
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,000
And we both know

140
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:56,560
that the three of us are all we have as a family.

141
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,520
No matter what happens,

142
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,160
we'll protect each other.

143
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,240
Yes, Auntie.

144
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,560
And Kit, I trust you know

145
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:12,160
what needs to be done to put an end
to this problem as quickly as possible

146
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,680
for the three of us.

147
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:16,240
I'll do as you say, Mom.

148
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:22,960
I'm glad my son still has a clear head
and knows what he needs to do.

149
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:29,520
All right, then that's what we'll do.

150
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,440
I'll meet with the fortune teller
to pick the wedding date

151
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:36,280
and the event organizer to discuss the wedding.

152
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:40,280
We won't invite outsiders to the wedding

153
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,720
except Punnapat.

154
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:45,680
And the only other guests will be family members.

155
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:49,680
Everyone will understand that
the wedding is being held to ward off bad luck.

156
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,640
That's settled, then.

157
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,320
As for the two of you,

158
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,480
get yourselves mentally and physically prepared.

159
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:01,280
And when you have time, practice being a couple.

160
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:04,320
Practice being a couple?

161
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,080
Of course.

162
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:11,480
We need to convince Punnapat that
Kit isn't the kind of man he thinks he is.

163
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,120
So everything has to look real.

164
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,040
When...

165
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,320
should we practice?

166
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,400
You don't have to go along
with everything she says.

167
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,200
Okay.

168
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,320
(Wedding Day)

169
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,840
I'll do my best today.

170
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:09,040
Nont! Nont, dear! Nont!

171
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,200
- Yes?
- It's Kit. He's gone.

172
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,280
He's not in his room and his car is gone.

173
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:15,240
And I checked the security footage.

174
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,280
He drove off early this morning.

175
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:21,520
Nont, I know he isn't happy about the wedding,

176
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:23,960
but I never thought he'd actually run away.

177
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:26,280
- Auntie, please calm down.
- And now the wedding...

178
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,400
Look at this first.

179
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:30,680
If he was really running away,

180
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:32,400
he wouldn't have taken such a small bag.

181
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,280
You're right.

182
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,760
Then where did he go, Nont?

183
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,880
How about this?

184
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,480
Go and wait at the wedding venue.

185
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,680
I'll go get Kit myself.

186
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,840
And do you know where he went?

187
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,800
I think so.

188
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:08,800
Kit.

189
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,760
You left without telling anyone.

190
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,720
Aunt Wan is worried sick.

191
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,640
I ran away just like she thought.

192
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,640
If you were really going to run,
you'd be much farther away by now.

193
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:27,280
I think right now,
you just don't know what to do next.

194
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,200
You really know me well.

195
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,920
You asked me to live with you.

196
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:35,120
If I don't know you, then who would I know?

197
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:39,280
Then you should know that
I don't want you getting involved in this.

198
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:47,600
Is there a better option than this?

199
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,280
You should have a life of your own.

200
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,120
Not take on my problems.

201
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,520
I'm not taking them on.

202
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,080
I'm willing.

203
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:57,840
But we may face a lot more problems.

204
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,280
Kit.

205
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:03,920
You said it yourself.

206
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:09,040
We may not have had a choice
in how our lives turned out before,

207
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,680
but from now on,

208
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,440
we can choose to be happy.

209
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,040
I've made my choice.

210
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,120
There's two hours left before the ceremony starts.

211
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,000
I'll see you at the wedding.

212
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,240
Big brother.

213
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:45,280
Thank you.

214
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,440
I'm the one who should be thanking you.

215
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:02,160
Dear family members and distinguished guests,

216
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,440
please join us in witnessing the marriage of

217
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:09,120
Mr. Kittipat Auttawarakul
and Mr. Nontawat Wasupang today,

218
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:14,040
as they both begin a new chapter in their lives.

219
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,640
As an orphan,

220
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,640
I never thought I'd have a day like this

221
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:26,640
where I get to stand beside him openly,

222
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,000
even if it's only an act.

223
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,400
I,

224
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,640
Nontawat Wasupang,

225
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,520
promise

226
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:40,440
to take care of and stand by

227
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:43,320
Kittipat Auttawarakul,

228
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,160
in good times

229
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,640
and bad times.

230
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:52,440
I, Kittipat Auttawarakul,

231
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:57,200
promise to take care of Nontawat Wasupang,

232
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:59,200
in good times

233
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:00,880
and bad times.

234
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:29,880
♪ I've heard a thousand stories ♪

235
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:34,800
♪ But it never crossed my mind ♪

236
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:42,200
♪ That my heart couldn't take
A world where you're not around ♪

237
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:53,520
♪ 'Cause I'm so sure that you're my world ♪

238
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:03,800
♪ I need you to know that after all... ♪

239
00:20:21,338 --> 00:20:23,738
Thank you so much for coming to my son's wedding.

240
00:20:24,218 --> 00:20:27,378
You went to the trouble of sending me
an invitation, as you promised.

241
00:20:28,098 --> 00:20:29,538
Of course I had to come.

242
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,298
Hello, ma'am.

243
00:20:35,498 --> 00:20:36,938
Congratulations.

244
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:39,698
Thank you, dear.

245
00:20:40,538 --> 00:20:43,298
Mr. Kittipat and Mr. Nontawat,

246
00:20:43,298 --> 00:20:45,898
please sign your marriage certificates.

247
00:21:01,978 --> 00:21:06,298
(Marriage Certificate)

248
00:21:16,058 --> 00:21:17,858
Congratulations to you both.

249
00:21:18,338 --> 00:21:20,698
And I hope everything will be settled,

250
00:21:22,538 --> 00:21:24,698
so our families have nothing to worry about.

251
00:21:25,298 --> 00:21:28,058
Thank you for coming to support us.

252
00:21:30,618 --> 00:21:32,818
And I hope we hold no more grudges.

253
00:21:36,138 --> 00:21:38,058
Excuse us while we take family photos.

254
00:21:53,778 --> 00:21:54,938
Smile, please. Smile.

255
00:21:55,418 --> 00:21:56,498
One, two...

256
00:22:04,538 --> 00:22:06,138
I'm sorry. Just a moment.

257
00:22:06,138 --> 00:22:07,578
Just a second, please.

258
00:22:09,618 --> 00:22:12,618
That bastard Pat is still here. Do as I say.

259
00:22:15,698 --> 00:22:17,538
Please take some couple photos.

260
00:22:17,538 --> 00:22:18,378
You got it.

261
00:22:19,658 --> 00:22:22,178
Nont, kiss him on the cheek, dear.

262
00:22:28,738 --> 00:22:30,178
Ah, just like that.

263
00:22:30,178 --> 00:22:31,178
Beautiful.

264
00:22:33,218 --> 00:22:35,578
Next photo. I want a kiss.

265
00:22:37,498 --> 00:22:38,618
A real kiss.

266
00:22:43,738 --> 00:22:44,738
Hold still.

267
00:22:47,698 --> 00:22:48,778
I'll do it.

268
00:22:56,578 --> 00:22:57,658
Hold it right there.

269
00:22:58,738 --> 00:22:59,578
Beautiful.

270
00:23:04,538 --> 00:23:07,098
So this is the man
you were willing to give it all up for.

271
00:23:12,538 --> 00:23:13,978
Good. One more, please.

272
00:23:14,858 --> 00:23:15,858
Okay.

273
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:19,858
Very well.

274
00:23:20,618 --> 00:23:22,458
At least now I know what you chose.

275
00:23:23,898 --> 00:23:24,698
Let's go home.

276
00:23:29,698 --> 00:23:30,418
Come on.

277
00:23:42,818 --> 00:23:43,778
Aunt Wan.

278
00:23:44,578 --> 00:23:47,578
I think registering the marriage is enough.

279
00:23:47,978 --> 00:23:49,858
We don't need the bedding ceremony.

280
00:23:50,698 --> 00:23:52,858
It'll just make Kit uncomfortable.

281
00:23:55,058 --> 00:23:57,778
I thought the same thing at first.

282
00:23:57,778 --> 00:23:59,578
And what happened? The power went out.

283
00:24:00,098 --> 00:24:02,698
See? Even God is warning us, son.

284
00:24:02,698 --> 00:24:05,178
It's because we do things halfway.

285
00:24:05,818 --> 00:24:06,858
Exactly.

286
00:24:06,858 --> 00:24:09,338
Auspicious ceremonies need to be done properly.

287
00:24:09,338 --> 00:24:11,418
That way, the bad things will fade away.

288
00:24:11,418 --> 00:24:15,738
And it'll also keep Mr. Kit safe from harm.

289
00:24:18,538 --> 00:24:19,658
This is overkill.

290
00:24:20,778 --> 00:24:21,658
Kittipat.

291
00:24:22,498 --> 00:24:27,258
Hey, the fact that you're still alive means
you've almost used up all your good karma.

292
00:24:28,098 --> 00:24:31,138
I'm not going to let bad luck come back to you.

293
00:24:32,098 --> 00:24:35,018
And if you ask me
who's sacrificed the most for this,

294
00:24:35,338 --> 00:24:36,298
it's him.

295
00:24:36,818 --> 00:24:37,978
Nont.

296
00:24:37,978 --> 00:24:42,018
He suddenly had to take on the responsibility
of helping his brother escape danger.

297
00:24:42,018 --> 00:24:43,778
- Kit, think about it.
- Aunt Wan.

298
00:24:44,698 --> 00:24:46,618
It's time. Let's start the ceremony.

299
00:24:47,298 --> 00:24:50,898
Please both get on the bed
and receive your mother's blessing.

300
00:25:05,458 --> 00:25:09,858
I wanted today to be the day
you both begin a new life.

301
00:25:12,618 --> 00:25:13,618
Kit.

302
00:25:14,658 --> 00:25:16,818
Now that Nont is your life partner,

303
00:25:18,178 --> 00:25:22,458
you have to love him,
take care of him, and cherish him, son.

304
00:25:23,978 --> 00:25:25,538
In a marriage,

305
00:25:25,538 --> 00:25:27,738
you must take care of each other.

306
00:25:28,698 --> 00:25:30,538
The three of us are all we have.

307
00:25:31,898 --> 00:25:33,498
Don't hurt each other's feelings.

308
00:25:36,858 --> 00:25:37,978
And Nont,

309
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:40,498
from now on,

310
00:25:40,498 --> 00:25:42,338
listen to Kit, okay?

311
00:25:48,578 --> 00:25:49,738
Yes, Aunt Wan.

312
00:25:50,378 --> 00:25:51,978
Don't call me Aunt anymore.

313
00:25:54,018 --> 00:25:55,298
Call me Mama.

314
00:25:56,898 --> 00:25:57,858
I will,

315
00:25:58,618 --> 00:25:59,738
Mama Wan.

316
00:26:04,218 --> 00:26:06,098
This is only the beginning.

317
00:26:11,178 --> 00:26:12,618
No matter what happens,

318
00:26:14,418 --> 00:26:16,578
I'll always be there for you two.

319
00:26:21,378 --> 00:26:24,178
All right, I've done my part for today.

320
00:26:25,058 --> 00:26:28,378
I'll go now, so the two of you can get some rest.

321
00:26:34,738 --> 00:26:36,098
Oh, I almost forgot.

322
00:26:36,898 --> 00:26:39,618
I had the hotel chef prepare
something special for you.

323
00:26:40,538 --> 00:26:42,658
Don't forget to eat my food, okay?

324
00:26:44,018 --> 00:26:47,578
And don't forget to put on
the pajamas I prepared for you.

325
00:26:51,098 --> 00:26:51,778
I'm off.

326
00:27:08,698 --> 00:27:11,578
Wow, if I eat all this,
my cholesterol's definitely going up.

327
00:27:13,578 --> 00:27:15,098
Something else will go up first.

328
00:27:16,338 --> 00:27:18,138
I'm not hungry. I'm taking a shower.

329
00:27:37,578 --> 00:27:38,618
Jeez.

330
00:27:44,378 --> 00:27:45,338
Kit.

331
00:27:46,418 --> 00:27:47,458
Look.

332
00:27:48,138 --> 00:27:49,538
The PJs from your mom.

333
00:27:51,418 --> 00:27:52,858
They're matching, too.

334
00:27:56,978 --> 00:27:58,338
Come here, let me help.

335
00:28:36,858 --> 00:28:38,418
Undo the top button for me, too.

336
00:28:38,418 --> 00:28:40,378
It's too tight. I can't breathe.

337
00:28:42,018 --> 00:28:43,058
Mm.

338
00:28:43,698 --> 00:28:44,658
Okay.

339
00:28:55,698 --> 00:28:56,498
Nont.

340
00:28:57,058 --> 00:28:59,098
There's no one watching us here.

341
00:28:59,578 --> 00:29:01,298
You can relax.

342
00:29:01,298 --> 00:29:03,418
No need to act in love all the time.

343
00:29:10,378 --> 00:29:11,258
Okay.

344
00:29:14,658 --> 00:29:16,658
Today's performance is over.

345
00:29:16,658 --> 00:29:18,618
Tomorrow, we go back to our old lives.

346
00:29:38,418 --> 00:29:39,778
I wasn't acting.

347
00:29:59,018 --> 00:29:59,938
Nont.

348
00:30:01,018 --> 00:30:01,938
Ow.

349
00:30:02,738 --> 00:30:03,978
What's wrong, Kit?

350
00:30:14,298 --> 00:30:15,378
Uh, Kit...

351
00:30:18,898 --> 00:30:22,778
What's the big deal?
You act like you've never seen it.

352
00:30:23,178 --> 00:30:25,898
We used to take showers together
after swimming lessons.

353
00:30:26,298 --> 00:30:27,898
What are you even talking about?

354
00:30:28,578 --> 00:30:29,778
I'm taking a shower.

355
00:30:30,298 --> 00:30:32,498
Wait. Where are you running off to?

356
00:30:33,658 --> 00:30:36,098
Hey, Kit. Kit.

357
00:30:37,778 --> 00:30:38,898
What are you doing?

358
00:31:22,356 --> 00:31:23,356
Kit.

359
00:31:25,036 --> 00:31:26,156
What are you doing?

360
00:31:27,596 --> 00:31:29,996
Nont, do you know why I agreed to marry you?

361
00:31:30,916 --> 00:31:31,916
Why?

362
00:31:32,276 --> 00:31:36,516
Because you told me that
your happiness comes from being with me,

363
00:31:36,516 --> 00:31:38,196
taking care of me,

364
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:39,796
and making me happy.

365
00:31:41,236 --> 00:31:44,276
Kit, I didn't say that last part.

366
00:31:44,756 --> 00:31:47,796
You don't have to say it.
I can see it in your eyes.

367
00:31:50,996 --> 00:31:54,556
I'll show you just how happy I can make you.

368
00:31:55,276 --> 00:31:56,796
Kit, what are you doing?

369
00:31:56,796 --> 00:31:58,076
Kit, no, no.

370
00:31:58,076 --> 00:31:59,396
Kit, no.

371
00:31:59,916 --> 00:32:01,436
Kit, Kit, no.

372
00:32:01,436 --> 00:32:02,996
Kit, no.

373
00:32:03,476 --> 00:32:05,436
Kit, Kit, Kit, Kit.

374
00:32:06,756 --> 00:32:07,996
Kit, no.

375
00:32:08,876 --> 00:32:09,716
Nont.

376
00:32:11,556 --> 00:32:12,596
Were you dreaming?

377
00:32:15,676 --> 00:32:16,516
Yes.

378
00:32:17,636 --> 00:32:19,636
What was it about? You were acting weird.

379
00:32:21,076 --> 00:32:21,956
Uh...

380
00:32:22,916 --> 00:32:24,076
I don't remember.

381
00:32:24,636 --> 00:32:26,876
I was tired. My dream was all over the place.

382
00:32:28,716 --> 00:32:29,836
Are you sick?

383
00:32:32,276 --> 00:32:33,756
I'm fine.

384
00:32:34,876 --> 00:32:36,236
Thanks for the concern.

385
00:32:37,316 --> 00:32:39,756
Then go take a shower so we can get some sleep.

386
00:32:43,076 --> 00:32:44,196
Go take a shower.

387
00:32:46,956 --> 00:32:47,916
Okay.

388
00:33:19,436 --> 00:33:20,356
Oh.

389
00:33:20,356 --> 00:33:23,076
Sorry. That was mine. I thought I was alone.

390
00:33:23,636 --> 00:33:24,436
Mm.

391
00:33:24,436 --> 00:33:25,476
Sorry.

392
00:33:25,796 --> 00:33:28,876
It's okay. I'm not used to it either.

393
00:33:30,076 --> 00:33:31,956
Kit? Where are you going?

394
00:33:34,596 --> 00:33:35,436
Kit.

395
00:33:40,276 --> 00:33:41,476
Where are you going?

396
00:33:41,836 --> 00:33:43,036
I'm going for a run.

397
00:33:43,596 --> 00:33:44,436
Right now?

398
00:33:44,436 --> 00:33:47,316
Yeah, right now. It's not hot outside.

399
00:33:52,956 --> 00:33:53,996
Wanna come with me?

400
00:33:57,156 --> 00:33:58,236
Do you want me to?

401
00:33:58,236 --> 00:34:00,116
Of course. I could use a running buddy.

402
00:34:02,036 --> 00:34:02,836
Let's go.

403
00:34:04,676 --> 00:34:06,236
Give it here. I'll do it.

404
00:34:16,996 --> 00:34:20,556
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

405
00:34:20,556 --> 00:34:23,916
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

406
00:34:23,916 --> 00:34:26,596
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

407
00:34:26,596 --> 00:34:30,956
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

408
00:34:30,956 --> 00:34:34,196
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

409
00:34:34,196 --> 00:34:38,556
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

410
00:34:38,556 --> 00:34:42,716
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

411
00:34:43,676 --> 00:34:47,636
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

412
00:34:47,636 --> 00:34:51,156
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

413
00:34:51,156 --> 00:34:57,236
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

414
00:34:57,236 --> 00:35:00,756
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

415
00:35:00,756 --> 00:35:04,356
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

416
00:35:04,996 --> 00:35:06,636
Let's do just 10K today.

417
00:35:08,236 --> 00:35:09,716
You call that "just"?

418
00:35:10,756 --> 00:35:11,636
What was that?

419
00:35:12,636 --> 00:35:13,556
I said...

420
00:35:14,276 --> 00:35:15,636
I'll stretch you out.

421
00:35:19,796 --> 00:35:20,596
Mm.

422
00:35:25,916 --> 00:35:26,876
Lift your leg.

423
00:35:33,516 --> 00:35:36,716
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

424
00:35:36,716 --> 00:35:41,116
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

425
00:35:41,116 --> 00:35:44,716
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

426
00:35:44,716 --> 00:35:45,716
Here, right?

427
00:35:47,236 --> 00:35:48,716
You really know me well.

428
00:35:50,196 --> 00:35:52,396
♪ Today, I've finally realized that love ♪

429
00:35:52,396 --> 00:35:53,436
Both sides.

430
00:35:53,836 --> 00:35:57,916
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

431
00:35:57,916 --> 00:35:58,716
Feels good.

432
00:35:59,836 --> 00:36:02,956
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

433
00:36:02,956 --> 00:36:03,756
How's that?

434
00:36:04,396 --> 00:36:05,196
Good.

435
00:36:07,236 --> 00:36:09,996
♪ Being close to you makes me dream about you ♪

436
00:36:11,156 --> 00:36:13,516
Come on. Let me do yours.

437
00:36:13,996 --> 00:36:17,236
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

438
00:36:17,236 --> 00:36:20,516
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

439
00:36:20,516 --> 00:36:25,156
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

440
00:36:25,156 --> 00:36:27,756
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

441
00:36:27,756 --> 00:36:30,756
♪ That says I love you? ♪

442
00:36:31,156 --> 00:36:34,076
♪ Love you ♪

443
00:36:35,676 --> 00:36:36,596
Feels okay?

444
00:36:38,316 --> 00:36:39,636
Feels great.

445
00:36:55,116 --> 00:36:56,076
Nont.

446
00:36:56,836 --> 00:36:58,196
Is your brain awake yet?

447
00:37:00,356 --> 00:37:01,356
Yes, it is.

448
00:37:02,876 --> 00:37:05,476
If it's about you, I'm always ready to listen.

449
00:37:09,236 --> 00:37:10,436
About the marriage,

450
00:37:11,156 --> 00:37:14,076
thank you for marrying me to help me out.

451
00:37:16,596 --> 00:37:18,876
But I want you to keep this a secret.

452
00:37:19,676 --> 00:37:20,596
Don't tell anyone.

453
00:37:22,516 --> 00:37:24,636
Even if it's just to ward off bad luck.

454
00:37:29,916 --> 00:37:30,796
Sure.

455
00:37:31,316 --> 00:37:34,076
It's not like I have anyone to tell anyway.

456
00:37:34,636 --> 00:37:35,556
Good.

457
00:37:36,356 --> 00:37:38,356
I don't wanna get you into any more trouble.

458
00:37:39,276 --> 00:37:41,116
But I want that trouble.

459
00:37:41,116 --> 00:37:42,356
Hm? What was that?

460
00:37:42,836 --> 00:37:44,076
No, nothing.

461
00:37:45,636 --> 00:37:46,796
Whoa, Kit.

462
00:37:47,676 --> 00:37:48,796
I completely forgot.

463
00:37:49,636 --> 00:37:51,316
Mama Wan wants us at breakfast.

464
00:37:56,116 --> 00:37:57,276
Thank you.

465
00:37:57,276 --> 00:37:59,436
Could you take this away? I'm not eating.

466
00:37:59,756 --> 00:38:00,596
No.

467
00:38:01,996 --> 00:38:05,476
Having only a cup of coffee
for breakfast is not healthy.

468
00:38:06,556 --> 00:38:08,956
Mama Wan, Kit is fasting.

469
00:38:09,276 --> 00:38:11,316
He can't eat until after two.

470
00:38:12,316 --> 00:38:14,476
Skipping breakfast because it's trendy?

471
00:38:15,396 --> 00:38:17,396
You've been fooled by social media.

472
00:38:17,396 --> 00:38:20,116
Mom, there are studies supporting it.

473
00:38:20,796 --> 00:38:22,196
It's healthy, too.

474
00:38:24,156 --> 00:38:25,716
Alright, okay, okay.

475
00:38:26,196 --> 00:38:27,596
Suit yourself.

476
00:38:27,596 --> 00:38:29,756
Everyone's an adult here, after all.

477
00:38:31,356 --> 00:38:34,236
But right now, you're in my house.

478
00:38:35,156 --> 00:38:37,196
So you have to follow my rules.

479
00:38:37,996 --> 00:38:39,436
I like having breakfast,

480
00:38:39,996 --> 00:38:43,196
so the two of you have to eat with me.

481
00:38:45,836 --> 00:38:47,156
What a dictator.

482
00:38:48,196 --> 00:38:49,076
Uh, I'll do it.

483
00:38:50,196 --> 00:38:51,796
I'll eat with you, Mama.

484
00:38:54,036 --> 00:38:57,996
See? My Nont is such a sweet boy.

485
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:00,916
Unlike my biological son.

486
00:39:01,676 --> 00:39:02,716
Fine.

487
00:39:02,716 --> 00:39:05,236
Your biological son is gonna eat right now, Mom.

488
00:39:05,236 --> 00:39:06,396
I'll do it.

489
00:39:08,236 --> 00:39:09,516
That's my boy.

490
00:39:09,516 --> 00:39:11,476
And after we finish,

491
00:39:11,476 --> 00:39:13,236
you two are coming with me.

492
00:39:13,236 --> 00:39:14,516
I have something to show you.

493
00:39:14,516 --> 00:39:15,796
Can we do it another day?

494
00:39:16,596 --> 00:39:18,076
I need to be at the office today.

495
00:39:18,836 --> 00:39:20,076
What is this?

496
00:39:20,396 --> 00:39:23,516
Kit, you haven't even been
married to Nont for 24 hours,

497
00:39:23,516 --> 00:39:25,276
and you're leaving him for work?

498
00:39:25,276 --> 00:39:26,836
Absolutely not. I won't allow it.

499
00:39:27,796 --> 00:39:30,676
After we finish here, you're coming with me.

500
00:40:40,097 --> 00:40:41,977
What do you think? Is it beautiful?

501
00:40:42,937 --> 00:40:44,417
It's gorgeous, Mama Wan.

502
00:40:45,377 --> 00:40:48,257
A house this big must've cost a fortune.

503
00:40:49,497 --> 00:40:50,817
Not that much.

504
00:40:51,777 --> 00:40:53,257
Just a little over a hundred.

505
00:40:55,137 --> 00:40:56,217
A hundred million?

506
00:40:57,097 --> 00:40:58,177
A hundred million.

507
00:41:00,897 --> 00:41:02,337
Do you two like it?

508
00:41:05,977 --> 00:41:07,417
Why are there photos of me?

509
00:41:08,497 --> 00:41:10,937
I asked if you like it or not.

510
00:41:10,937 --> 00:41:12,577
Just answer the question.

511
00:41:13,577 --> 00:41:14,457
I like it.

512
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:16,057
What about you, Nont?

513
00:41:16,497 --> 00:41:17,297
I like it.

514
00:41:18,937 --> 00:41:20,977
I'm glad you both like it.

515
00:41:22,377 --> 00:41:24,817
I bought this house...

516
00:41:24,817 --> 00:41:26,377
as a wedding gift.

517
00:41:29,417 --> 00:41:30,497
A wedding gift?

518
00:41:34,017 --> 00:41:36,257
You really didn't have to go this far.

519
00:41:37,017 --> 00:41:40,097
I want the two of you
to have your own private space,

520
00:41:41,137 --> 00:41:43,097
so you won't feel awkward or uncomfortable.

521
00:41:44,177 --> 00:41:46,737
But don't worry about me being lonely.

522
00:41:46,737 --> 00:41:48,857
If I get lonely, I'll drop by.

523
00:41:50,857 --> 00:41:53,737
I thought we agreed we were
only doing this to fix the problem.

524
00:41:54,337 --> 00:41:57,337
I already told you, if we're going to do this,

525
00:41:57,337 --> 00:41:58,937
we have to make it look real

526
00:41:58,937 --> 00:42:01,457
so Punnapat will be completely convinced.

527
00:42:01,817 --> 00:42:04,217
And a married couple needs a marital home.

528
00:42:15,057 --> 00:42:16,217
In this envelope,

529
00:42:16,737 --> 00:42:19,017
I've had a lawyer draw up a contract.

530
00:42:19,777 --> 00:42:22,097
If, within one year,

531
00:42:22,817 --> 00:42:25,617
you hurt Nont so badly
that you two end up divorcing,

532
00:42:25,617 --> 00:42:27,897
this house will immediately become Nont's.

533
00:42:28,697 --> 00:42:30,977
I'll deduct the cost from your account.

534
00:42:44,097 --> 00:42:48,257
You being like this is exactly
why I want to make my own fortune.

535
00:42:50,457 --> 00:42:52,577
So I can stop following your orders.

536
00:42:53,177 --> 00:42:55,257
Then prove it to me, Kit.

537
00:42:55,777 --> 00:42:59,097
Show me you're better than I am
and can run a business better than I can.

538
00:43:11,777 --> 00:43:13,337
Mama Wan, Mama Wan.

539
00:43:16,017 --> 00:43:18,097
Kit was just speaking out of anger.

540
00:43:18,097 --> 00:43:20,377
He didn't mean to hurt your feelings.

541
00:43:20,817 --> 00:43:21,857
I know, dear.

542
00:43:22,457 --> 00:43:24,377
I was pretty harsh with him, too.

543
00:43:25,897 --> 00:43:27,857
Ever since his father left me,

544
00:43:28,577 --> 00:43:30,377
I've only had Kit.

545
00:43:31,537 --> 00:43:33,337
And I'm afraid that one day,

546
00:43:33,857 --> 00:43:35,257
I'll lose him too.

547
00:43:39,457 --> 00:43:40,377
Mama Wan.

548
00:43:41,457 --> 00:43:42,617
Don't be afraid.

549
00:43:44,177 --> 00:43:45,977
He doesn't show it often,

550
00:43:46,937 --> 00:43:49,697
but I believe he loves you very much.

551
00:43:53,257 --> 00:43:53,977
Nont.

552
00:43:55,057 --> 00:43:56,617
Don't ever leave Kit, dear.

553
00:43:58,857 --> 00:44:02,097
And I'm entrusting this house to you.

554
00:44:06,417 --> 00:44:07,657
I promise.

555
00:44:08,937 --> 00:44:10,497
No matter what happens,

556
00:44:11,617 --> 00:44:13,257
I'll always stand by him.

557
00:44:16,217 --> 00:44:17,257
Thank you, dear.

558
00:44:18,777 --> 00:44:19,577
Come on.

559
00:44:20,377 --> 00:44:23,177
So, how was it? Did you sleep well last night?

560
00:44:23,497 --> 00:44:24,537
I slept really well.

561
00:44:25,617 --> 00:44:28,057
Oh, and what's going on with your luck?

562
00:44:28,057 --> 00:44:29,977
Something always gets in the way.

563
00:44:29,977 --> 00:44:33,377
The power went out right at
the crucial moment yesterday.

564
00:44:35,297 --> 00:44:37,737
Mama Wan, don't worry.

565
00:44:38,137 --> 00:44:39,737
Everything will work itself out.

566
00:44:40,097 --> 00:44:41,017
Okay?

567
00:44:41,337 --> 00:44:42,337
Thank you, dear.

568
00:44:42,657 --> 00:44:43,937
I should get going.

569
00:44:44,657 --> 00:44:47,017
Oh, don't walk me out. I can manage.

570
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,537
Go take care of Kit.

571
00:44:49,257 --> 00:44:50,217
- Okay.
- I'm off.

572
00:44:50,217 --> 00:44:51,217
- See you.
- See you.

573
00:44:52,937 --> 00:44:55,937
Mama Wan, everyone's luck is different.

574
00:44:56,617 --> 00:44:58,777
You see the power going out as bad omen.

575
00:45:00,097 --> 00:45:01,417
But for me,

576
00:45:02,777 --> 00:45:04,497
it's a fortunate thing.

577
00:45:07,977 --> 00:45:12,377
Kit, you're the one who stages
this power outage, aren't you?

578
00:45:13,937 --> 00:45:14,777
Yes.

579
00:45:17,537 --> 00:45:19,257
When do you want me to do it?

580
00:45:19,257 --> 00:45:21,017
When the MC says

581
00:45:21,457 --> 00:45:23,297
the married couple should kiss.

582
00:45:38,697 --> 00:45:42,217
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

583
00:45:42,217 --> 00:45:45,617
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

584
00:45:45,617 --> 00:45:48,257
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

585
00:45:48,257 --> 00:45:52,617
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

586
00:45:52,617 --> 00:45:55,817
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

587
00:45:55,817 --> 00:46:00,217
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

588
00:46:00,217 --> 00:46:04,497
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

589
00:46:05,377 --> 00:46:08,737
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

590
00:46:09,297 --> 00:46:12,817
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

591
00:46:12,817 --> 00:46:15,457
♪ Is something I should get to know ♪

592
00:46:15,457 --> 00:46:16,697
What's on your mind?

593
00:46:18,217 --> 00:46:18,897
Nothing.

594
00:46:18,897 --> 00:46:22,417
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

595
00:46:22,417 --> 00:46:24,937
So we're really going to be living here.

596
00:46:26,257 --> 00:46:29,097
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

597
00:46:29,097 --> 00:46:30,417
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

598
00:46:30,417 --> 00:46:32,857
♪ You cracked my code ♪

599
00:46:32,857 --> 00:46:36,297
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

600
00:46:36,297 --> 00:46:39,537
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

601
00:46:39,537 --> 00:46:44,177
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

602
00:46:44,177 --> 00:46:46,817
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

603
00:46:46,817 --> 00:46:49,617
♪ That says I love you? ♪

604
00:47:10,777 --> 00:47:11,577
What are you looking at?

605
00:47:13,697 --> 00:47:14,857
- Hey, no.
- Whoa.

606
00:47:14,857 --> 00:47:16,177
Why is it so high, Nont?

607
00:47:16,177 --> 00:47:18,177
Every time my heart starts racing,

608
00:47:18,177 --> 00:47:20,257
Kit is always close by.

609
00:47:20,257 --> 00:47:23,417
This is the first time
my heart has raced this hard.

610
00:47:23,417 --> 00:47:25,737
I've diagnosed myself.

611
00:47:25,737 --> 00:47:27,057
I'm falling in love.

612
00:47:29,097 --> 00:47:31,137
Want me to help relieve your stress?

613
00:47:31,777 --> 00:47:33,177
Go all out, then.

614
00:47:33,177 --> 00:47:34,577
Just try to keep up, then.

615
00:47:35,937 --> 00:47:39,737
♪ When closeness starts to stir up feelings ♪

616
00:47:39,737 --> 00:47:46,937
♪ And my heart starts to get carried away ♪

617
00:47:46,937 --> 00:47:50,497
♪ As our bond begins to change ♪

618
00:47:50,497 --> 00:47:52,697
♪ Every time I look at you ♪

619
00:47:52,697 --> 00:47:55,057
♪ My heart ♪

620
00:47:55,777 --> 00:47:59,017
♪ Flutters more than I can bear ♪

621
00:47:59,417 --> 00:48:02,097
♪ Before I knew it ♪

622
00:48:02,097 --> 00:48:04,817
♪ Before I realized how I felt ♪

623
00:48:04,817 --> 00:48:08,137
♪ I couldn't stop it anymore ♪

624
00:48:08,137 --> 00:48:11,377
♪ It's too late now ♪

625
00:48:11,377 --> 00:48:17,017
♪ I'm already yours ♪

626
00:48:18,977 --> 00:48:22,337
♪ Somehow I gave my heart to you ♪

627
00:48:22,657 --> 00:48:28,337
♪ I don't even know when it happened ♪

628
00:48:29,737 --> 00:48:33,057
♪ Someone who's always here ♪

629
00:48:33,057 --> 00:48:38,017
♪ Someone you know so well ♪

630
00:48:38,497 --> 00:48:43,937
♪ There's something I've been waiting to say ♪

631
00:48:43,937 --> 00:48:49,377
♪ But I don't know how to say it ♪

632
00:48:51,617 --> 00:48:55,297
♪ Being by your side like this ♪

633
00:48:55,297 --> 00:48:59,497
♪ Makes me feel so good that I still... ♪
